<title>NETHERLANDS: BADMINTON-DUTCH OPEN SEMIFINAL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BADMINTON-DUTCH OPEN SEMIFINAL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>DEN BOSCH, Netherlands 1996-10-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Open</p>
<p>semifinal results on Saturday:</p>
<p>Men's singles</p>
<p>Poul-Erik Hoyer Larsen (Denmark) beat Gang Cheng (China) 11-8</p>
<p>6-9 9-6 9-2</p>
<p>Jun Sun (China) beat Darren Hall (England) 9-2 3-9 9-5 9-4</p>
<p>Note: The Dutch Open is the first grand prix tournament to</p>
<p>play the best-of-five shortened games, each to nine points</p>
<p>instead of the best-of-three 15-point games.</p>
</text>
